<Item XName="Step01-Scenario1_RCS_Main" UserName="Step01-Scenario1_RCS_Main" Type="Equation">
<AutoCalc><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></AutoCalc>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>%% This Equation contains the basic configurations for Vehicle RCS Test-Scenario No.1&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Reference Paper: &#x000D;&#x000A;% I. Matsunami, R. Nakamura, A. Kajiwara. &#x000D;&#x000A;% RCS Measurements for Vehicles and Pedestrians at 26 and 79 GHz, &#x000D;&#x000A;% 2012-International Conf. on SigProcess and CommSys, IEEE.&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%%Preliminary RCS Data Setups&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Scenario Setup Mode Selection&#x000D;&#x000A;Scenario_Setup = 01; %% &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%% RCS Output Settings&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce01_No_Tgts = 5; %% Total target numbers (from 0 to 10)&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce01_Freq_Band = 02; %% 01 for 26 GHz, 02 for 79 GHz&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce01_RCS_Type = [02, 01, 04, 05, 01]; %% 01-05: Sedan, Small Van, Bicycle, Manned Bicycle, Pedestrian;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce01_RCS_ValueSel = [01, 02, 03, 02, 01]; %% 01 for maximum, 02 for mean, and 03 for minimum;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%%RCS Output as SquareMeters&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce01_RCS = RCS_Output_VehicleSce1(Scenario_Setup, Sce01_No_Tgts, Sce01_Freq_Band, Sce01_RCS_Type, Sce01_RCS_ValueSel);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="EquationDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;p14;GR14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;SWh1k68Yl24;OPTbrLKRN24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Split><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split>
<Split2><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split2>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;45;R2;8A;u4</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>4</D></ZOrder></Item></Item>
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Step01-Scenario2_RCS_Main" UserName="Step01-Scenario2_RCS_Main" Type="Equation">
<AutoCalc><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></AutoCalc>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>%% This Equation contains the basic configurations for Vehicle RCS Test-Scenario No.2&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Reference Paper: &#x000D;&#x000A;% K.Geary, Joseph S. Colburn, etc., (Joint work by HRL Lab and General Motors)&#x000D;&#x000A;% Automotive Radar Target Characterization from 22 to 29 GHz and 76 to 81 GHz &#x000D;&#x000A;% 2013-IEEE Radar Conference.&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%%Preliminary RCS Data Setups&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Scenario Setup Mode Selection&#x000D;&#x000A;Scenario_Setup = 02; %% &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%% RCS Output Settings&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce02_No_Tgts = 6; %% Total target numbers (from 0 to 10)&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce02_Freq_Band = 02; %% 01 for 22-29 GHz, 02 for 76-81 GHz&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce02_RCS_Type = [01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06]; %% 01-06: Sedan (Cadillac STS), Truck (Chevrolet Avalanche), Van (Chevrolet Express), Bicyclist, Motorist, Adult Pedestrian;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce02_RCS_ValueSel = [02, 02, 02, 02, 02, 02]; %% 01 for Back/Front Peak, 02 for Oblique Peak (if any), 03 for Side Peak, 04 for Minimum;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%%RCS Output as SquareMeters&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce02_RCS = RCS_Output_VehicleSce2(Scenario_Setup, Sce02_No_Tgts, Sce02_Freq_Band, Sce02_RCS_Type, Sce02_RCS_ValueSel);&#x0009;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="EquationDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;GY14;G04</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;l6uQWhTIU24;evTctPUZA14</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Split><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split>
<Split2><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split2>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;;1;1</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>11</D></ZOrder></Item></Item>
<Item XName="VarBlock" Type="VarBlock" /></Item>
<Item XName="Step01-Scenario3_RCS_Main" UserName="Step01-Scenario3_RCS_Main" Type="Equation">
<AutoCalc><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></AutoCalc>
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>%% This Equation contains the basic configurations for Vehicle RCS Test-Scenario No.3&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Reference Paper: &#x000D;&#x000A;% Emna Bel Kamel, Alain Peden, Patrice Pajusco, etc., (By Telocom Bretagne MO, Lab-STICC)&#x000D;&#x000A;% RCS Modeling and Measurements for Automotive Radar Applications in the W Band&#x000D;&#x000A;% 2017-11th European Conf. on Antennas and Propagation (EuCAP).&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%%Preliminary RCS Data Setups&#x000D;&#x000A;%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%&#x000D;&#x000A;%% Scenario Setup Mode Selection&#x000D;&#x000A;Scenario_Setup = 03; %% &#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%% RCS Output Settings&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce03_No_Tgts = 7; %% Total target numbers (from 0 to 10)&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce03_Freq_Band = 02; %% 01 for 22-29 GHz NOT Available, 02 for 76-81 GHz&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce03_RCS_Type = [01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06, 07]; %% 01-07: Van (Renault Trafic), Small Van (Peugeot 5008), Sedan(Peugeot 406), Small Sedan(Peugeot 107), Luxury Sedan (Alfa Romeo Giulietta), Bicycle, Pedestrian.  &#x000D;&#x000A;Sce03_RCS_ValueSel = [01, 02, 03, 04, 01, 02, 02]; %% 01 for Back/Front Peak, 02 for Oblique Peak (if any), 03 for Side Peak, 04 for Minimum;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;%%RCS Output as SquareMeters&#x000D;&#x000A;Sce03_RCS = RCS_Output_VehicleSce3(Scenario_Setup, Sce03_No_Tgts, Sce03_Freq_Band, Sce03_RCS_Type, Sce03_RCS_ValueSel);&#x0009;&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
<Name>Courier New</Name>
<Size><T>Double</T><D>125</D></Size></Item>
<Item XName="FunctionBlock" Type="FunctionBlock" />
<Item XName="Page" Type="PageMgr">
<Item XName="Display0" Type="EquationDisp">
<DVport><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;p14;ea14</D></DVport>
<PVPort><T>Array_Dbl64</T><D>1;4;;;SWh1k68Yl24;PnY5BMN7X24</D></PVPort>
<Show><T>Bool</T><D>1</D></Show>
<ShowCmd><T>Int</T><D>1</D></ShowCmd>
<Split><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split>
<Split2><T>Double</T><D>0.3</D></Split2>
<Window><T>Array_I64</T><D>1;4;;W6;45;m9</D></Window>
<ZOrder><T>Int</T><D>2</D></ZOrder></Item></Item>
